 "standard_text": "2A.7G rewrite radical expressions that contain variables to equivalent forms; 2A.7H solve equations involving rational exponents",
 "meta_desc": "Free Algebra II worksheets for Texas TEKS 2A.7G and 2A.7H: simplify square, cube and fourth roots with variables, rational exponents and solving rational exponent equations. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "x^(m/n) = ⁿ√(x^m).",
 "key_sub": "Solve x^(m/n) = c by raising both sides to n/m.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li><i>x</i><sup><i>m</i>/<i>n</i></sup> = <sup><i>n</i></sup>√(<i>x</i><sup><i>m</i></sup>) = (<sup><i>n</i></sup>√<i>x</i>)<sup><i>m</i></sup>: the denominator is the root, the numerator is the power.</li><li>To simplify an <i>n</i>th root, take out groups of <i>n</i>: ∛(<i>x</i><sup>7</sup>) = <i>x</i><sup>2</sup>∛<i>x</i>.</li><li>To solve <i>x</i><sup><i>m</i>/<i>n</i></sup> = <i>c</i>, raise both sides to the reciprocal power <i>n</i>/<i>m</i>.</li><li>If <i>m</i> is even, there are two answers (±).</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'><i>x</i><sup>3/2</sup> = 27</p><p class='sn-ex-s'><i>x</i> = 27<sup>2/3</sup></p><p class='sn-ex-s'>∛27 = 3, 3<sup>2</sup> = 9</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 9</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>∛(16<i>x</i><sup>5</sup>)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>16 = 8 · 2, <i>x</i><sup>5</sup> = <i>x</i><sup>3</sup> · <i>x</i><sup>2</sup></p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 2<i>x</i>∛(2<i>x</i><sup>2</sup>)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dividing by 2 for a cube root</td><td>For ∛, take out groups of 3.</td></tr><tr><td>Swapping the parts of the exponent</td><td><i>x</i><sup>2/3</sup> is ∛(<i>x</i><sup>2</sup>).</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting ±</td><td><i>x</i><sup>2/3</sup> = 4 gives <i>x</i> = ±8.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
